rcial aggregators were not scraped, BDL site returns 403 to scripted access)."}, {"id": "fx_sayrafa_milestones", "label": "BDL Sayrafa platform rate, selected dates, 2021-2023", "unit": "LBP/USD", "topic": "fx", "freq": "daily", "source_url": "https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=1&ptype=1", "license": null, "points": [["2021-05-20", 12000], ["2021-09-08", 16000], ["2021-10-11", 16000], ["2021-11-30", 20600], ["2021-12-27", 23200], ["2022-02-16", 20400], ["2022-12-16", 30800], ["2022-12-28", 38000], ["2022-12-29", 38000], ["2023-01-09", 38000], ["2023-02-28", 45400], ["2023-03-02", 70000], ["2023-03-13", 75800], ["2023-03-20", 83500], ["2023-03-21", 90000], ["2023-03-31", 90000], ["2023-04-03", 88000], ["2023-04-06", 87000], ["2023-04-19", 86700], ["2023-07-14", 85500], ["2023-07-31", 85500], ["2023-12-19", 89500]], "notes": "Sparse sample (not a complete daily history) of the Sayrafa rate that BDL published in daily press releases; BDL site is public but states no open licence (license null), values are public facts quoted with source. Platform announced 10 May 2021, first reference rate 12,000 (20 May 2021); from 1 Feb 2022 the Sayrafa rate applied to card payments; 2023-03-21 BDL set 90,000 and bought lira; 89,500 platform rate from 19 Dec 2023, replaced by the official 89,500 in Feb 2024. Per-point provenance: 2021-05-20: BDL governor statement of 20 May 2021 (the961.com/lebanon-central-bank-lbp-usd-rate-12000-sayrafa; L'Orient-Le Jour 21 May 2021) | 2021-09-08: BDL statement, volume-weighted average, https://www.banqueduliban.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=4773 | 2021-10-11: BDL statement via lebanontoday.net 2021-10-11 | 2021-11-30: BDL statement via arabbanks.net 2021-11-30 | 2021-12-27: BDL statement via lebanontoday.net 2021-12-27 | 2022-02-16: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=29&ptype=1 | 2022-12-16: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=6693 | 2022-12-28: https://www.banqueduliban.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=6740 | 2022-12-29: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=6742 | 2023-01-09: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=14&ptype=1&tpages=35 | 2023-02-28: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7054 | 2023-03-02: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7092 | 2023-03-13: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7106 | 2023-03-20: https://www.banqueduliban.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7116 | 2023-03-21: L'Orient Today 21 Mar 2023 (BDL raised from 83,500 to 90,000) | 2023-03-31: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7173 | 2023-04-03: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7175 | 2023-04-06: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7196 | 2023-04-19: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease1.php?pressid=7253 | 2023-07-14: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=1&ptype=1 (flat 85,500 daily from 14 to 31 Jul 2023) | 2023-07-31: https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=1&ptype=1 | 2023-12-19: BDL 'Platform Rate for 19/12/2023', https://www.bdl.gov.lb/pressrelease.php?page=1&ptype=1. The full daily BDL Excel file (bdl.gov.lb/sayrafa.php) was not downloadable by script (HTTP 403); fetching it is a refresh task."}, {"id": "fx_bank_rate_lollar", "label": "BDL \"bank rate\" for USD deposit withdrawals in LBP (Circular 151), step changes", "unit": "LBP/USD", "topic": "fx", "freq": "daily", "source_url": "https://bdl.gov.lb/CB%20Com/Laws%20And%20Regulations/Basic%20Circulars/Decision_13221_EN%C2%A73813_3.pdf", "license": null, "points": [["2020-04-21", 3900], ["2021-12-09", 8000], ["2023-02-01", 15000]], "notes": "Step series (value holds until next point). 3,900: Basic Circular 151 / Decision 13221 of 21 Apr 2020 (Byblos Bank FAQ, Executive Magazine); 8,000: Intermediate Circular 601 of 9 Dec 2021 for USD 3,000/month, valid to 30 Jun 2022 (Blominvest 10 Dec 2021; The National 9 Dec 2021; Libnanews), extended later; 15,000 from 1 Feb 2023 (LBCI 31 Jan 2023; current text of Decision 13221 sets 15,000, limit USD 1,600/month, until 31 Dec 2023). Circular 166 (Feb 2024) replaced the scheme with USD 150 monthly cash withdrawals (AUB Outlook, 21 Feb 2024)."}, {"id": "fx_official_peg_steps", "label": "Official BDL peg / reference rate, step changes since 1997", "unit": "LBP/USD", "topic": "fx", "freq": "irregular", "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebanese_pound", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0 (Wikipedia) for the regime summary; underlying BDL decisions public", "points": [["1997-12", 1507.5], ["2023-02-01", 15000], ["2024-01-31", 89500]], "notes": "Step series. 1,507.5 fixed from December 1997 (Wikipedia; IMF IFS end-of-period shows 1,507.5 by 1998; some sources date the peg to 1999). 15,000 effective 1 Feb 2023 (statement by governor Salameh to Reuters on 31 Jan 2023, BDL website change; L'Orient Today 7 Feb 2024). 89,500: BDL Central Council decision 48/4/24 dated 15 Feb 2024 adopted 89,500 in the BDL balance sheet from 31 Jan 2024 (Credit Libanais https://economics.creditlibanais.com/Article/212041); L'Orient Today 7 Feb 2024 says circular 167 treats 89,500 as the single reference rate; FAOSTAT shows 89,500 for Jan 2024. CORRECTION 2026-10-02 (V2 verification): first point was dated 1997-12; hub's own FAOSTAT monthly shows 1,527.91 in Dec 1997 and first 1,507.5 in 1999-01 (World Bank annual 1997 = 1,539.45, 1998 = 1,516.13), so the step is dated 1999-01 (peg announced Dec 1997, in force at 1,507.5 from 1999; press and Wikipedia still say 1997). The 89,500 step is dated by its effective date 2024-01-31 (previously 2024-02-15, the date of BDL decision 48/4/24); confidence medium: press confirms 89,500 adopted by 15 Feb 2024, the 31 Jan effective date rests on the Credit Libanais note above. 89,500 on 2023-12-19 is the Sayrafa platform rate, a separate series (fx_sayrafa_milestones), not the official rate. Official series: 1,507.5 to 31 Jan 2023, 15,000 from 1 Feb 2023, 89,500 from 31 Jan 2024; Jul-Dec 2023 = 15,000 (matches FAOSTAT). Peg fixed at LL 1,507.5 from December 1997 (BDL policy; Wikipedia 'Lebanese pound', ANND); the annual average official rate first equals 1,507.5 in 1999 (World Bank PA.NUS.FCRF), because late-1997 and 1998 averages still include the convergence to the peg. (Corrected back from a 1999-01 start set by a fixer.)"}, {"id": "fx_customs_rate", "label": "Ministry of Finance customs dollar rate, selected change", "unit": "LBP/USD", "topic": "fx", "freq": "daily", "source_url": "https://reliefweb.int/report/lebanon/lebanon-crisis-update-may-2023", "license": null, "points": [["2023-05-12", 86000]], "notes": "On 12 May 2023 the Ministry of Finance raised the customs dollar rate to 86,000 through 31 May 2023 (ReliefWeb Lebanon Crisis Update, May 2023, 8 Jun 2023). Other customs, NSSF and VAT rates were not collected."}]}